byid['1975-395.2']['statement']=r'''Let \(A=K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]\), with \(K\) a field, and let the row length be \(r\ge2\). A unimodular row gives a split surjection \(A^r\to A\), whose kernel is finitely generated projective. Its freeness gives an invertible matrix completing the row; rescaling one other row makes the determinant one. For row length one, a unit is the only entry, and determinant one requires that unit to equal one.'''
